<!--

Super-Kamiokande 2023 Data Fit Configuration — PRODUCTION (V1c+V3, 2026-08-29)

Event-engine projection of the user-adopted V1c+V3 production systematic-prior
set (sheet of record: claude/2-atmospheric-oscillation/SuperK/dm2-shift-causes/
sk_production_priors.pdf; adoption ruling: SK2017_PRIOR_CROSSWALK_2026-08-28.md
section "ADOPTION (2026-08-29, USER RULING)"). Derived from
SK2023_Atm_datafit_phased_upmufix_fluxfix.xml with the production widths
applied wherever the event framework has the corresponding base dial.

MC base of record: SuperK_fullMC_7_2_x100.h5 (MC 7.2, x100 => MCexposure 100).

Width changes vs the parent XML (all from the validated V3 runner env,
RM_SIGMA_SET in WARD claude-tmp/pablo_mc_diff/run_v3_scan.sh):
  XSecNuTau            0.20 -> 0.25   (SK-2017 paper width)
  CC_2p2h              1.00 -> 0.10   (paper; was 10x inflated)
  CC_2p2hNuBarNu       1.00 -> 0.10   (paper; was 10x inflated)
  zenith_up            0.02 -> 0.01   (paper)
  zenith_down          0.02 -> 0.01   (paper)
  fcpc_separation      0.06 -> 0.01   (production merged single dial, PE prior)
  upmu_shower_separation 0.04 -> 0.012 (0.3x tightening of the spec width;
                        engine runs this era-split: 0.0102/0.0132/0.0072/0.009
                        for sk1/sk2/sk3/sk45 — base dial carries 0.3 x 0.04)
  upmu_stop_bkg        0.17 -> 0.007  (V1c repurposed split stop-reduction
                        norm; engine era-split 0.007/0.007/0.007/0.005 —
                        base dial carries the loosest-era envelope)
  upmu_showering_bkg   0.17 -> 0.005  (V1c thru-showering reduction norm;
                        engine era-split 0.005/0.005/0.005/0.003)
  upmu_nonshowering_bkg 0.24 -> 0.005 (V1c thru-nonshowering reduction norm;
                        engine era-split 0.005/0.005/0.005/0.003)

Deliberately UNCHANGED base dials (production changes not representable here):
  flavor_ratio 0.02   — production PINS this dial, superseded by the banded
                        sum-preserving flux_flavor_{subgev,mid,high} engine
                        dials at paper widths 0.02/0.03/0.05; the event engine
                        has no banded flux dials, so the base dial stays FREE
                        at the sub-GeV paper width to preserve flavor freedom.
  nunubar_ratio 0.05  — same story: production uses banded sum-preserving
                        flux_numubar_{subgev,mid,high} = 0.02/0.06/0.15 and
                        flux_nuebar_{subgev,mid,high} = 0.05/0.05/0.08.
  pc_reduction 0.02   — production tightens only the sk3 era copy to 0.009
                        (paper); the base era-common dial keeps the spec width.
  decay_e_tagging 0.10 — already at the paper width in the parent XML.

Engine-only production elements with NO event-framework counterpart (live in
the binned engine spec/env, see run_v3_scan.sh): upmu_norm (single up-mu
normalization, PINNED), the 3 horizon-bin up-mu background shape dials
(upmu_stop_bkg_horiz_lowp 0.090 / _highp 0.036, upmu_nonshow_bkg_horiz 0.013,
FLOATING), the clean CCQE shape basis (xsec_ccqe_shape_subgev 0.40 +
xsec_ccqe_shape_multigev 0.20 ACTIVE, global power-law xsec_ccqe_shape
RETIRED/pinned at nominal), kpi_ratio 0.10, updown_escale_sk2/sk3 0.006/0.013,
and the 12 whole-sample upmu_*_bkg_{era} norms pinned at nominal.

Oscillation parameters (dCP, Sin2Theta13, Sin2Theta12, Dm221) are profiled
programmatically in the row worker, not scanned in XML.
-->
